# Line endings are part of the build here, not a preference.
#
# The Windows runner checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` unless told
# otherwise, and three checks compare bytes: `prettier --check`,
# `cargo fmt --check` and `tools/protocol.mjs check`, which diffs freshly
# generated Go/TypeScript against the committed files. Any of them fails on a
# CRLF working copy. Normalising to LF in the repository and on checkout keeps
# the three platforms byte-identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never text, whatever the heuristic decides.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.bin binary
*.db binary
